```python
def bubble_sort(nums):
    result = list(nums)
    n = len(result)
    for i in range(n - 1):
        swapped = False
        for j in range(0, n - i - 1):
            if result[j] > result[j + 1]:
                result[j], result[j + 1] = result[j + 1], result[j]
                swapped = True
        if not swapped:
            break
    return result
```

This code introduces a flag `swapped` to track whether any swaps were made in the inner loop. If no swaps were made, it means the list is already sorted and the algorithm can terminate early, reducing the time complexity to O(n^2) in the best case.
